{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>The name of the one</b>. The Gaon [Saadia] said that Pishon is the Nile of Egypt. It is known that Gihon is near the Land of Israel, as it is written, \"and you shall bring him down to Gihon\" (1 Kings 1:33), and it comes from the southeast. So too the Euphrates, and it is the easternmost boundary of the land on the eastern side. The commentators said that the Tigris is the second river, the one that flows past Baghdad along with the Euphrates river. If so, the three of them are all eastern, and the Nile of Egypt emerges from the Mountain of Frankincense, far from the equator on the southern side, and the proof is great in summer. We know that Eden was on the equator, so that the day neither increases nor decreases all the days of the year. Those devoid of understanding — how is this possible, when the proofs are complete and without doubt upon them? If so, Pishon descends to the southwest and then turns back northward. But there is no proof that Pishon is the Nile — only that he translated Havilah according to his need, for he has no received tradition. So too he did with the families, and the regions, and the animals, and the birds, and the stones. Perhaps he saw it in a dream, and he has already erred in some of them, as I shall explain in its place. If so, we do not rely on his dreams. Perhaps he did so for the honor of HaShem, because he translated the Torah into the language of Ishmael and in their script, so that they would not say that there are commandments in the Torah that we do not know. And he mentioned the gold on account of the honor of the river that emerges from the Garden."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Reading 'הזהב' (the gold) with the sense 'he mentioned the gold'; the clause is compressed and the subject of 'הזכיר' is inferred as the verse/scripture, not the Gaon."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:52.130545491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}